# =============================================================================
# Frontend variable catalog. There is one variable, and it is deliberately not
# set anywhere.
#
# Vite bakes every VITE_* variable into the PUBLIC bundle, so none of them can
# ever hold a secret and there is no .env.local here. Vite names its files
# after the build mode, so overrides would be .env.development /
# .env.production, not .env.dev / .env.prod.
# =============================================================================

# VITE_API_URL      Secret: no.  Default: /api/v1
#                   Base URL of the API. The default is relative on purpose:
#                   the browser then always talks to the origin it loaded the
#                   page from, and nothing needs CORS. The Vite dev server
#                   proxies /api to localhost:3000, and nginx proxies the same
#                   path in the container, so the default is already right in
#                   both. That is why no env file sets it.
#                   Set it to an absolute URL only if you deploy the frontend
#                   on a different origin from the API, and add that origin to
#                   CORS_ORIGIN on the API side when you do.
